  "caveats": [
    "CVE-2026-96889 is also assigned by the Next.js developer to its upstream image-optimization advisory. Preserve Librsvg and Next.js as distinct affected packages within this same-CVE record; neither package version range substitutes for the other.",
    "Librsvg CNA assesses High/CVSS 3.1 7.8 for its upstream context, while the Next.js wrapper developer assesses Critical with its own CVSS 4.0 vector. These are source- and deployment-specific assessments, not interchangeable scores.",
    "GNOME release NEWS confirms fixes in 2.57.5, 2.60.3, 2.61.5, 2.62.4 and 2.63.2. Affected branch boundaries retain Reviewed/RustSec attribution. Release-page publication dates were not independently established and remain null.",
    "Next.js requires the affected image-optimization path on glibc Linux and recommends sharp>=0.35.5 or its corresponding Next.js patches. An upstream CVE is not evidence of exploitation in the wild."
  ],
